export anchor PulpSciFiStyle:
    number: 142
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Pulp sci-fi
    idea: A 1950s pulp magazine printed in two inks on yellowed paper, where the greeting is a cover headline with a starburst, projects are the contents page and progress is a little ship on a dashed flight path.
    base: light
    palette:
        pulp: #f4e4c1, the page
        page: #fbf1da, cover, panels and text on ink
        redInk: #b5121b, masthead band, starburst, Behind and the primary button
        navyInk: #1a2a5e, header, frames, On track and At risk
        keyBlack: #1c1a24, body text and hard shadows
        greyInk: #4d4a5a, small labels
        halftone: #b5121b, red or navy dots at 16 to 18 percent as cover and chart texture
    type:
        Masthead and headlines use Impact, Haettenschweiler, Arial Narrow
        Bold, Oswald in caps, slanted minus 6 to 10 degrees. Labels use
        Franklin Gothic Medium, Arial Narrow in caps tracked 0.08em. Body
        uses Century Schoolbook, TeX Gyre Schola, Georgia. Masthead up to
        92px, headline up to 58px, numbers 40px, contents titles 19px bold
        italic serif, body 16px at 1.5.
    layout:
        A navy header holds a slanted brand, a paper search, a red New
        project with a raygun and hard shadow, a round bell and the user,
        over a red nav where the current item is paper with a raygun. The
        cover sits left in a 6px navy frame with a red masthead band, a
        week and date price box, a navy tagline strip and a halftone scene
        with a rocket and ringed planet, the date, a huge slanted greeting,
        a red starburst for 4 tasks overdue and four callout boxes with hard
        shadows. In this issue sits right as a contents list numbered 01 to
        06 in red, with italic serif names, category and due, a dashed
        flight path with a red trail and a ship at the percent, and tasks
        with status. Below are Dispatches from the crew with red time tags
        and a bar chart of rocket nosed bars, striped navy last week and
        solid red this week.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 12 to 18px inside panels, 28px between cover and contents.
    density: Busy cover, orderly contents list, big type everywhere.
    corners: Square. Curves only in planets, rockets and the starburst.
    borders: Thick ink frames, 6px navy on the cover, 3px black on panels, 2px dotted navy between entries.
    shadows: Hard offset 4px solid shadows in navy, red or black, like misregistered print.
    icons: Two ink silhouettes. Rocket On track, ringed planet At risk, comet Behind, red starburst for overdue, a raygun on the primary button and current nav item.
    focus: A 3px navy outline offset 3px, then a paper gap and a red ring.
    tone: Breathless cover lines with exclamation marks, such as In this issue, Dispatches from the crew and Launches per day.
